  "summary": "The root cause is that when an ideating item encounters an exception (e.g., JSON parse error, rate limit error, or file I/O failure), it gets added to `_auto_plan_queued` in tui.py but is never removed because `_on_plan_done()` is only called on successful completion, not on exceptions. This creates a permanent blockage: subsequent `_auto_plan_check()` calls skip the queued item (line ~3484), and since the loop breaks after picking the first candidate, no other ideating items get processed either. The 5-minute rate-limit backoff is fixed (not exponential), so progressive backoff isn't the issue — the real problem is items getting permanently stuck in the queue after errors. The fix should: (1) move `_auto_plan_queued.discard(slug)` into a `finally` block in `_run_ideating_async()` so items are always cleaned up, (2) handle corrupted/empty feature files gracefully by skipping them rather than letting them block the entire queue, and (3) continue iterating over remaining candidates when one fails instead of breaking after the first match."
